				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://cfs.nrcan.gc.ca/fc-data-catalogue</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The Forest Climate Change Data Catalogue is a collection of data sets that are relevant to the Canadian forest sector under a changing climate. Created by Canadian Forest Service scientists, these data sets include static maps, raw data, and interactive maps that cover all of Canada. Data themes include drought, fire, climate and tree distribution; multiple climate scenarios are projected to the year 2100. The data sets will be periodically updated as new information becomes available.</r3d:description>
